MetaParser v2 Implementation Plan:

Architecture Principle:
  MetaParser is a PURE SOURCE GENERATOR with ZERO runtime dependency.
  All code that runs in the user's application is GENERATED, not referenced.

  Phase 1 - Schema V2 Models (Generator-side):
    ✔ Create Schema/TokenDefinition.cs @done
    ✔ Create Schema/SchemaDefinition.cs @done
    ✔ Create Schema/PatternDefinition.cs @done
    ✔ Create Schema/SchemaValidator.cs @done
    ✔ Update Generator.cs for v2 schema parsing @done
    Tests:
      ✔ Test schema deserialization @done
      ✔ Test pattern parsing @done
      ✔ Test validation errors @done

  Phase 2 - Code Generation Infrastructure:
    ✔ Create Generation/CodeBuilder.cs (StringBuilder wrapper with indentation) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/GeneratedFileBuilder.cs (file header, namespace, usings) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/SourceProductionContextExtensions.cs (helper to add sources) @done
    Tests:
      ✔ Test CodeBuilder indentation @done
      ✔ Test GeneratedFileBuilder produces valid C# @done

  Phase 3 - Green Node Code Generation:
    ✔ Create Generation/GreenNodeGenerator.cs (emits GreenNode base class) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/GreenTriviaGenerator.cs (emits GreenTrivia classes) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/GreenTokenGenerator.cs (emits GreenToken variants) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/GreenTokenFactoryGenerator.cs (emits factory with caching) @done
    Generated output includes:
      - GreenNode (IFormattable, ISpanFormattable)
      - GreenTrivia, GreenTriviaList
      - GreenTokenWithNoTrivia, WithLeadingTrivia, WithTrailingTrivia, WithTrivia
      - GreenTokenFactory with keyword caching
      - All format specifiers (T, C, M, D, J, G)
    Tests:
      ✔ Test generated GreenNode compiles @done
      ✔ Test generated IFormattable works @done
      ✔ Test all generators use correct namespace @done
    Integration Tests (compile generated code and run):
      ✔ Test GreenTrivia string/memory construction @done
      ✔ Test GreenTrivia ToOwned @done
      ✔ Test GreenTriviaList width calculation @done
      ✔ Test GreenTokenWithNoTrivia properties @done
      ✔ Test GreenTokenWithLeading/TrailingTrivia widths @done
      ✔ Test GreenTokenWithTrivia all trivia @done
      ✔ Test GreenTokenFactory caching behavior @done
      ✔ Test IFormattable T/C/M/D/J/G formats @done
      ✔ Test source reconstruction @done

  Phase 4 - TokenKind & Consumer Code Generation:
    ✔ Create Generation/TokenKindGenerator.cs (emits TokenKind enum from schema) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/ConsumerInterfaceGenerator.cs (emits IConsumer, ILexerConsumer) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/SequenceReaderExtensionsGenerator.cs (emits SIMD helpers) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/TokenConsumerGenerator.cs (emits consumer per token) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/LexerGenerator.cs (emits lexer orchestrator) @done
    Generated output includes:
      - TokenKind enum with all token types
      - ITokenConsumer interface with SequenceReader<char>
      - SequenceReaderExtensions (TryReadExact, AdvanceWhile, etc.)
      - Per-token consumer classes
      - Lexer class with Tokenize() method
    Tests:
      ✔ Test generated TokenKind enum has all tokens @done
      ✔ Test generated consumer interface compiles @done
      ✔ Test generated lexer tokenizes simple input @done

  Phase 5 - Trivia Attachment Code Generation:
    ✔ Create Generation/TriviaAttachmentGenerator.cs (emits trivia splitting logic) @done
    Generated output includes:
      - TriviaAttacher class (Roslyn-compatible trivia splitting)
    Tests:
      ✔ Test generated trivia attaches to following token @done
      ✔ Test generated trivia splits at newline @done

  Phase 6 - Red Node Code Generation:
    ✔ Create Generation/RedNodeGenerator.cs (emits RedNode wrapper) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/RedTokenGenerator.cs (emits RedToken wrapper) @done
    Generated output includes:
      - RedNode (lazy wrapper with Parent, Position)
      - RedToken (token wrapper with span access)
      - TextSpan struct for span representation
    Tests:
      ✔ Test generated RedNode parent navigation @done
      ✔ Test generated RedNode position calculation @done

  Phase 7 - Full Parser Code Generation:
    ✔ Create Generation/ParserGenerator.cs (emits full parser class) @done
    ✔ Create Generation/SyntaxTreeGenerator.cs (emits SyntaxTree class) @done
    Generated output includes:
      - Parser class (lexer + trivia + tree building)
      - SyntaxTree (root accessor, diagnostics)
      - Diagnostic and DiagnosticSeverity classes
      - GreenTokenList for flat token streams
    Tests:
      ✔ Test generated parser produces valid tree @done
      ✔ Test generated parser round-trips source @done

  Phase 8 - Schema Analysis with Dependency Graphs:
    ✔ Create Graphs/GraphEdge.cs (simple edge struct) @done
    ✔ Create Graphs/DirectedGraph.cs (adjacency list implementation) @done
    ✔ Create Graphs/CycleDetection.cs (DFS-based cycle detection) @done
    ✔ Create Graphs/TopologicalSort.cs (Kahn's + DFS algorithms) @done
    ✔ Create Schema/TokenDependencyAnalyzer.cs (builds token reference graph) @done
    ✔ Update SchemaValidator.cs to detect circular references @done
    Features:
      - Build directed graph of token → pattern → token references
      - Detect circular dependencies (error diagnostic)
      - Detect unreachable tokens (warning diagnostic)
      - Compute optimal token generation order
    Tests:
      ✔ Test DirectedGraph add/query operations @done
      ✔ Test CycleDetection for acyclic/cyclic graphs @done
      ✔ Test TopologicalSort for dependency ordering @done
      ✔ Test TokenDependencyAnalyzer circular reference detection @done
      ✔ Test TokenDependencyAnalyzer unreachable token detection @done
      ✔ Test SchemaValidator circular dependency integration @done

  Phase 9 - Diagnostics:
    ☐ Create Diagnostics/DiagnosticDescriptors.cs (v2 diagnostic definitions)
    Tests:
      ☐ Test diagnostic for invalid schema
      ☐ Test diagnostic location accuracy

  Phase 10 - Integration Testing:
    ☐ Create test project that consumes generated code
    Tests:
      ☐ Test simple calculator schema end-to-end
      ☐ Test string literal with escapes
      ☐ Test trivia preservation
      ☐ Test incremental generation

Dependencies:
  - Custom Graphs library (Graphs/ folder, inspired by Graffs)

Target Frameworks:
  Generator: netstandard2.0 (required for Roslyn)
  Generated Output: net8.0+ (C# 12, SearchValues<char>)

